  "summary": "A PICU fellow talks with a mother about worsening respiratory failure, what returning home could mean, and how palliative care can support her family.",
  "scenario": "Eli Johnson is a 9 YO boy with severe hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, epilepsy, tracheostomy, and ventilator dependence. He was admitted to the PICU six days ago with severe pneumonia and acute-on-chronic respiratory failure. He initially stabilized but has not returned to his baseline ventilator settings. The team is worried he may not survive this admission or recover to his prior functional baseline.\n\nMarissa Johnson, Eli's mother and primary caregiver, has asked to speak with you after hearing the attending say \"We need to talk about the bigger picture.\" She is worried the team is giving up on Eli.",
